{"id":"rel.wave2.batch10.01","from_formulation":"form.wave2.foundation.reduced-ring","target_meaning":"meaning.wave2.foundation.associative-ring-identity-optional","relation_type":"definition_uses","review_state":"screened","source_phrase":"An associative ring R","editorial_reason":"A reduced ring is an associative ring in which nonzero nilpotent elements are excluded; the ring structure is prior, and no identity is imposed by the general source.","source_locator":"https://proofwiki.org/wiki/Definition%3AReduced_Ring","target_locator":"https://proofwiki.org/wiki/Definition%3ARing_%28Abstract_Algebra%29","reviewed_by":"assistant_independent_mathematical_source_comparison_2026_10_19","human_verified":false}
{"id":"rel.wave2.batch10.02","from_formulation":"form.wave2.foundation.ring-map-general","target_meaning":"meaning.wave2.foundation.associative-ring-identity-optional","relation_type":"definition_uses","review_state":"screened","source_phrase":"associative rings","editorial_reason":"A ring homomorphism is defined between associative rings and preserves both operations. The underlying ring axioms are needed before requiring that map compatibility.","source_locator":"https://proofwiki.org/wiki/Definition%3ARing_Homomorphism","target_locator":"https://proofwiki.org/wiki/Definition%3ARing_%28Abstract_Algebra%29","reviewed_by":"assistant_independent_mathematical_source_comparison_2026_10_19","human_verified":false}
{"id":"rel.wave2.batch10.03","from_formulation":"form.wave2.foundation.ring-map-general","target_meaning":"meaning.wave2.foundation.mapping-element-assignment","relation_type":"definition_uses","review_state":"screened","source_phrase":"φ:R→S","editorial_reason":"Every ring homomorphism is first a function from the underlying set of R to that of S, with additional addition and multiplication preservation.","source_locator":"https://proofwiki.org/wiki/Definition%3ARing_Homomorphism","target_locator":"https://proofwiki.org/wiki/Definition%3AMapping","reviewed_by":"assistant_independent_mathematical_source_comparison_2026_10_19","human_verified":false}
{"id":"rel.wave2.batch10.04","from_formulation":"form.wave2.foundation.ring-map-unital","target_meaning":"meaning.wave2.foundation.ring-map-general","relation_type":"definition_uses","review_state":"screened","source_phrase":"additive and multiplicative homomorphism","editorial_reason":"Unital ring homomorphisms are the identity-preserving special case of arbitrary ring homomorphisms. The general underlying operation-preserving map is prerequisite.","source_locator":"https://proofwiki.org/wiki/Definition%3ARing_Homomorphism","target_locator":"https://proofwiki.org/wiki/Definition%3ARing_Homomorphism","reviewed_by":"assistant_independent_mathematical_source_comparison_2026_10_19","human_verified":false}
{"id":"rel.wave2.batch10.05","from_formulation":"form.wave2.foundation.ring-map-unital","target_meaning":"meaning.wave2.foundation.associative-ring-identity-optional","relation_type":"definition_uses","review_state":"screened","source_phrase":"rings R and S","editorial_reason":"The definition of a unital ring homomorphism presupposes associative ring structures on both source and target, plus their respective multiplicative identities.","source_locator":"https://proofwiki.org/wiki/Definition%3ARing_Homomorphism","target_locator":"https://proofwiki.org/wiki/Definition%3ARing_%28Abstract_Algebra%29","reviewed_by":"assistant_independent_mathematical_source_comparison_2026_10_19","human_verified":false}
{"id":"rel.wave2.batch10.06","from_formulation":"form.wave2.foundation.well-ordered-set","target_meaning":"meaning.709d3d2f82950c5b.partially-ordered-set","relation_type":"definition_uses","review_state":"screened","source_phrase":"total order","editorial_reason":"Every well-ordered set is totally ordered and hence partially ordered; well-ordering adds least elements for all nonempty subsets.","source_locator":"https://proofwiki.org/wiki/Definition%3AWell-Ordered_Set","target_locator":"https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/002Z","reviewed_by":"assistant_independent_mathematical_source_comparison_2026_10_19","human_verified":false}
{"id":"rel.wave2.batch10.07","from_formulation":"form.wave2.foundation.well-ordered-set","target_meaning":"meaning.wave2.foundation.subset-nonstrict","relation_type":"definition_uses","review_state":"screened","source_phrase":"nonempty subset A⊆S","editorial_reason":"The well-order axiom quantifies over the nonempty subsets of S, so the general non-strict inclusion concept is a structural prerequisite.","source_locator":"https://proofwiki.org/wiki/Definition%3AWell-Ordered_Set","target_locator":"https://proofwiki.org/wiki/Definition%3ASubset","reviewed_by":"assistant_independent_mathematical_source_comparison_2026_10_19","human_verified":false}
{"id":"rel.wave2.batch10.08","from_formulation":"form.wave2.foundation.subspace-topology-general","target_meaning":"meaning.wave2.foundation.topological-space","relation_type":"definition_uses","review_state":"screened","source_phrase":"topological space","editorial_reason":"A subspace topology is constructed from an ambient topological space and its open sets; general topology is prior to the induced topology.","source_locator":"https://proofwiki.org/wiki/Definition%3ASubspace_Topology","target_locator":"https://proofwiki.org/wiki/Definition%3ATopological_Space","reviewed_by":"assistant_independent_mathematical_source_comparison_2026_10_19","human_verified":false}
{"id":"rel.wave2.batch10.09","from_formulation":"form.wave2.foundation.subspace-topology-general","target_meaning":"meaning.wave2.foundation.subset-nonstrict","relation_type":"definition_uses","review_state":"screened","source_phrase":"subset A⊆X","editorial_reason":"The induced topology requires a subset A of the original space as the underlying carrier before taking intersections with its open sets.","source_locator":"https://proofwiki.org/wiki/Definition%3ASubspace_Topology","target_locator":"https://proofwiki.org/wiki/Definition%3ASubset","reviewed_by":"assistant_independent_mathematical_source_comparison_2026_10_19","human_verified":false}
{"id":"rel.wave2.batch10.10","from_formulation":"form.wave2.foundation.subspace-topology-nonempty","target_meaning":"meaning.wave2.foundation.subspace-topology-general","relation_type":"definition_uses","review_state":"screened","source_phrase":"τ_A={A∩U:U∈τ}","editorial_reason":"The nonempty convention is a restriction of the general induced subspace construction; no separate topology operation is needed.","source_locator":"https://proofwiki.org/wiki/Definition%3ASubspace_Topology","target_locator":"https://proofwiki.org/wiki/Definition%3ASubspace_Topology","reviewed_by":"assistant_independent_mathematical_source_comparison_2026_10_19","human_verified":false}
{"id":"rel.wave2.batch10.11","from_formulation":"form.wave2.foundation.subspace-topology-nonempty","target_meaning":"meaning.wave2.foundation.topological-space","relation_type":"definition_uses","review_state":"screened","source_phrase":"(X,τ)","editorial_reason":"The restricted convention still requires the ambient topological space whose open sets determine its subspace topology.","source_locator":"https://proofwiki.org/wiki/Definition%3ASubspace_Topology","target_locator":"https://proofwiki.org/wiki/Definition%3ATopological_Space","reviewed_by":"assistant_independent_mathematical_source_comparison_2026_10_19","human_verified":false}
{"id":"rel.wave2.batch10.12","from_formulation":"form.6c51aeb904a0fe74.geometrically-reduced-algebra","target_meaning":"meaning.wave2.foundation.reduced-ring","relation_type":"definition_uses","review_state":"screened","source_phrase":"reduced ring","editorial_reason":"Geometric reducedness requires base-change algebras to be reduced rings. The general nilpotent-free ring property is prerequisite.","source_locator":"https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/05DS","target_locator":"https://proofwiki.org/wiki/Definition%3AReduced_Ring","reviewed_by":"assistant_independent_mathematical_source_comparison_2026_10_19","human_verified":false}
